cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference Pilotage, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Pilotage: an MCP extension for guided program authoring and verified execution"
abstract: >-
  Pilotage is an extension profile over the Model Context Protocol (MCP) that
  lets AI agents safely author and execute programs — SQL, automation rules,
  workflow documents — against any live system. It standardizes a small set of
  pieces expressed with MCP's own primitives: a manifest, navigable guides
  (the grammar), a versioned catalog (the live world), a mandatory
  side-effect-free validate verb returning structured diagnostics plus a
  pre-run plan with per-step risk, an execution trace carrying per-step
  inputs, outputs and branch decisions, and one standard client loop. Governing rule: standardize the
  loop, not the language.
